WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.910
“Britain’s best export,” I was told by the head of the Department of Immigration in Canberra, “is people.”
“英国最好的出口品，”堪培拉移民部的负责人对我说，“是人。”

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:18.750
Close on 100,000 people have applied for assisted passages in the first five months of this year, and half of these are eventually expected to migrate to Australia.
今年头五个月，已有近10万人申请了移民旅费资助，预计其中一半最终会移居澳大利亚。

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.210
The Australians are delighted.
澳大利亚人非常高兴。

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:32.950
They are keenly aware that without a strong flow of immigrants into the workforce the development of the Australian economy is unlikely to proceed at the ambitious pace currently envisaged.
他们深知，如果没有大批移民源源不断地进入劳动力队伍，澳大利亚经济就不太可能像目前雄心勃勃的设想那样高速发展。

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:52.680
The new mineral discoveries promise a splendid future, and the injection of huge amounts of American and British capital should help to ensure that they are properly exploited, but with unemployment in Australia down to less than 1.3 percent, the government is understandably anxious to attract more skilled labor.
新发现的矿藏预示着辉煌的前景，大量美国和英国资本的注入也应该有助于确保这些矿藏得到妥善开发；但由于澳大利亚的失业率已降至不足1.3%，政府急于吸引更多熟练劳动力，也就在情理之中了。

00:00:53.480 --> 00:01:00.490
Australia is roughly the same size as the continental United States, but has only twelve million inhabitants.
澳大利亚的面积与美国本土大致相当，但居民只有1200万。

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:10.420
Migration has accounted for half the population increase in the last four years, and has contributed greatly to the country’s impressive economic development.
过去四年里，人口增长有一半来自移民，移民还为这个国家令人瞩目的经济发展作出了巨大贡献。

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:21.280
Britain has always been the principal source—ninety percent of Australians are of British descent, and Britain has provided one million migrants since the Second World War.
英国一直是主要来源——90%的澳大利亚人是英国后裔，第二次世界大战以来，英国已经输送了100万移民。

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.380
Australia has also given great attention to recruiting people elsewhere.
澳大利亚也十分重视从其他地方招募人员。

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:36.440
Australians decided they had an excellent potential source of applicants among the so-called “guest workers” who have crossed their frontier to work in other parts of Europe.
澳大利亚人认定，那些越过自己国家的边境、到欧洲其他地区打工的所谓“客籍工人”，是潜在申请人的绝佳来源。

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:45.590
There were estimated to be more than four million of them, and a large number were offered subsidized passages and guaranteed jobs in Australia.
据估计，这些人有400多万，澳方为其中很多人提供了旅费补贴，并保证他们在澳大利亚有工作。

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:55.090
Italy has for some years been the second biggest source of migrants, and the Australians have also managed to attract a large number of Greeks and Germans.
几年来，意大利一直是第二大移民来源国，澳大利亚人还设法吸引到了大量希腊人和德国人。

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:02.700
One drawback with them, so far as the Australians are concerned, is that integration tends to be more difficult.
就澳大利亚人而言，这些移民有一个缺点：他们往往更难融入。

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:09.860
Unlike the British, continental migrants have to struggle with an unfamiliar language and new customs.
与英国人不同，欧洲大陆移民不得不努力应对陌生的语言和新的习俗。

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:17.680
Many naturally gravitate towards the Italian or Greek communities, which have grown up in cities such as Sydney and Melbourne.
很多人自然而然地投奔意大利人或希腊人社区，这些社区已经在悉尼、墨尔本等城市发展起来。

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.710
These colonies have their own newspapers, their own shops, and their own clubs.
这些聚居地有自己的报纸、自己的商店和自己的俱乐部。

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.040
Their inhabitants are not Australians, but Europeans.
这些聚居地的居民不是澳大利亚人，而是欧洲人。

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:38.190
The government’s avowed aim, however, is to maintain “a substantially homogeneous society into which newcomers, from whatever sources, will merge themselves.”
然而，政府公开宣称的目标是维持“一个基本同质的社会，无论新来者来自何处，都将融入其中”。

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:47.510
By and large, therefore, Australia still prefers British migrants, and tends to be rather less selective in their case than it is with others.
因此，总的来说，澳大利亚仍然偏爱英国移民，对英国移民的挑选往往也比对其他移民宽松不少。

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:56.780
A far bigger cause of concern than the growth of national groups, however, is the increasing number of migrants who return to their countries of origin.
然而，比各民族群体的壮大令人担忧得多的，是返回原籍国的移民人数日益增多。

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:08.010
One reason is that people nowadays tend to be more mobile, and that it is easier than in the past to save the return fare, but economic conditions also have something to do with it.
原因之一是，如今人们往往流动性更强，而且攒够回程路费也比过去容易了；不过，经济状况也与此有一定关系。

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:20.110
A slower rate of growth invariably produces discontent—and if this coincides with greater prosperity in Europe, a lot of people tend to feel that perhaps they were wrong to come here after all.
增长速度一放慢，总会引起不满——如果这时又恰逢欧洲更加繁荣，很多人往往就会觉得，也许当初到这里来终究是错了。

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:25.650
Several surveys have been conducted recently into the reason why people go home.
最近已就人们回国的原因开展了几项调查。

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:39.210
One noted that “flies, dirt, and outside lavatories” were on the list of complaints from British immigrants, and added that many people also complained about “the crudity, bad manners and unfriendliness of the Australians”.
其中一项调查指出，“苍蝇、尘土和户外厕所”都在英国移民的抱怨清单上，还补充说，很多人也抱怨“澳大利亚人的粗俗、无礼和不友好”。

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:47.920
Another survey gave climate conditions, homesickness, and “the stark appearance of the Australian countryside” as the main reasons for leaving.
另一项调查把气候条件、思乡之情以及“澳大利亚乡间荒凉的景象”列为离开的主要原因。

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:54.860
Most British migrants miss council housing, the national health scheme, and their relatives and former neighbors.
大多数英国移民都怀念市政公房、国民医疗保健制度，还有亲戚和以前的邻居。

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.180
Loneliness is a big factor, especially among housewives.
孤独是一大因素，在家庭主妇当中尤其如此。

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:06.490
The men soon make new friends at work, but wives tend to find it much harder to get used to a different way of life.
男人们很快就会在工作中交到新朋友，而妻子们往往会觉得，要适应另一种生活方式难得多。

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:18.560
Many are housebound because of inadequate public transport in most outlying suburbs, and regular correspondence with their old friends at home only serves to increase their discontent.
由于大多数偏远郊区的公共交通不够完善，她们当中许多人只能困在家里；而与国内老朋友定期通信，只会加深她们的不满。

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:25.040
One housewife was quoted recently as saying: “I even find I miss the people I used to hate at home.”
最近有报道援引一位家庭主妇的话说：“我甚至发现，自己想念起了以前在老家讨厌的那些人。”

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:30.150
Rents are high, and there are long waiting lists for Housing Commission homes.
房租很高，住房委员会公房的轮候名单很长。

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:35.680
Sickness can be an expensive business and the climate can be unexpectedly rough.
生病可能是件很花钱的事，气候也可能出人意料地恶劣。

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:44.890
The gap between Australian and British wage packets is no longer big, and people are generally expected to work harder here than they do at home.
澳大利亚和英国的工资差距已经不大了，而且一般来说，人们在这里需要比在国内工作得更卖力。

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:50.460
Professional men over forty often have difficulty in finding a decent job.
四十岁以上的男性专业人士往往很难找到一份像样的工作。

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:57.840
Above all, perhaps, skilled immigrants often find a considerable reluctance to accept their qualifications.
也许最重要的是，有技能的移民常常发现，人们相当不愿意认可他们的职业资格。

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:06.140
According to the journal Australian Manufacturer, the attitude of many employers and fellow workers is anything but friendly.
据《澳大利亚制造商》杂志称，许多雇主和同事的态度一点也不友好。

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:14.070
“We Australians,” it stated in a recent issue, “are just too fond of painting the rosy picture of the big, warm-hearted Aussie.
“我们澳大利亚人，”该杂志在最近一期中写道，“实在太喜欢把澳洲佬描绘成高大、热心肠的美好形象了。

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:22.270
As a matter of fact, we are so busy blowing our own trumpets that we have not got time to be warm-hearted and considerate.
事实上，我们忙着自吹自擂，忙得都没工夫热心待人、体贴别人了。

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:29.510
Go down ‘heart-break alley’ among some of the migrants and find out just how expansive the Aussie is to his immigrants.”
到一些移民当中去，走一走那条‘伤心巷’，看看澳洲佬对自己的移民究竟有多么热情豪爽吧。”
